Parliament did not ratify Tymosenko's release amendment
As part of an amendment to criminal law, Ukraine's parliament refused the draft annulment of the paragraph on the indictment of Julia Tymosenko, the leader of the opposition.
MPs refused at second reading the proposed amendment to reduce penalties for economic offenses, which could have opened the doors of freedom for the former Prime Minister currently imprisoned.
Tymosenko was sentenced in October to 7 years in prison for reaching a priori-disadvantaged agreement with Russia for the purchase of natural gas.
The judgment is not final and the court must rule on the appeal of the convict in December.
Tymosenko qualifies the regime's judgment as political revenge and has provoked a process of suspicions of partiality of the court also in the west.
The plan to annul paragraph 365 of criminal law, on the basis on which the former Prime Minister was convicted, was signed by 147 deputies.
It would have taken 226 votes to approve it.
Libyan Victory
The Libyan liberation or rebellion already has its vanquists.
Muammar Gaddafi is buried in an unfamilious place in the desert and without him the war is over.
It remains to determine the winners.
As is customary in the region, the winners in the elections are the Islamists, but these are moderates or radicals.
The Provisional National Council has decreed Sharia law and we already know what it is about.
Libya is becoming a country without crime because for a theft we cut our hands.
Women can forget emancipation, non-respects of the faith are punishable by capital punishment...
It is the Qur'an that will unite in place of the personality of the dictator the society composed of opposing tribes.
In Libya will reign such an order as we cannot represent it and as we would surely not like.
But our way of life is not unique, is not objectively the best and would probably not be beneficial for the Libyans.
It is especially surprising that Islamist warriors have gratefully accepted help from unfaithful dogs.
The only excuse is that it was not an American general who directed the NATO strikes but rather Allah whose greatness they celebrated with every attack.
So when it comes to looking for the winners in Libya, the West is not one of them
We participated in the shootings, served Islam, and our politicians turned away from the dictator as a political ally without this bringing any profit.
Following the recent bad experiences of Afghanistan and Iraq, we do not militarily occupy Libya.
So there is no problem for the locals to get rid of "crusaders".
Without land occupancy, the oil companies will have easy access to Libyian black gold.
Perhaps not so much and the West will finally be able to brag about the protection of human rights.
As long as these followers of Shariah prevent us.
A new era of crisis begins.
France and the rest of Europe are in the sights of investors.
A tornado of the statistics passed Tuesday on Europe.
Each of the states has published GDP-related information for 3As.
The Czech economy stagnated in the last quarter, while France and Germany are growing.
The bond market breaks all records.
Investors not only look at Italy, but also Spain, France, Austria and others.
The statistical offices of the eurozone, Germany, the Czech Republic and other countries in Europe published earlier their visions of economic development for the third quarter.
Germany's GDP has projected growth of 0.5%, that of France by 0.4%.
The two countries changed the data for the second quarter in which Germany placed better than expected (0.3% growth instead of 0.1% expected), however France reported a slight decrease of 0.1% (it was about stagnation).
The Czech economy grew by 1.5% in the third quarter.
But GDP has stagnated and according to the Czech Bureau of Statistics it is confirmed that we are moving towards a gradual decline in economic growth.
The results are worse than the forecasts of analysts.
The Most Important Events:
The Czech economy grew by 1.5% in the third quarter but stagnated during the last quarter.
In the third quarter, the German economy grew by 0.5% according to data forecast and recalculated periodically.
The economy of the eurozone and the European Union grew by 0.2% between July and September compared to the previous quarter, which corresponds to what analysts had predicted.
Greece’s economy fell by 5.2%.
The ten-year bond yield is 28.45%
Bond yields from Spain and Italy are climbing towards critical limits.
Problems are starting to feel in Austria, France, Belgium, etc...
Czech bond yields remain below 4% as the situation worsens in the region.
There are voices heard in Germany to say that the ECB should be the guarantee of the last instance .
The Czechs qualified for the EURO.
They won in Montenegro 1:0 and celebrate the qualification for 200 million
The representation of football has succeeded in its most difficult mission of the season!
In Montenegro, she also won thanks to Super Cech and goalkeeper Petr Jiracek 1:0.
Czech football has dearly defended with also a good share of luck in the second part its qualification and will not miss the European championship.
IHNED.cz followed the qualifying match with detailed reporting.
No particular excitement during the first part and a lot of luck for the second.
The Czech performance also won thanks to Super Cech and hero Petr Jiracek with 1:0 in Montenegro and celebrated his qualification for the European Championship.
The Montenegrains found themselves under pressure even in the second part because of a precise Czech defense.
The victims of the match were Damjanovic and Vucinic who missed two chances to score a goal.
And thanks to super Petr Cech the Czech representation will not be absent in the European championship next year, and in addition a reward of 200 million crowns in the coffer of Czech football.
From the first few minutes we played a warrior football.
The two teams were struggling to mount combinations and the game focused mainly around the center line.
Pressure from national footballers did not manage to break through the Czech defense, which responded precisely to the long shots even during the first half.
Iranian students are willing to die for their country’s nuclear program.
They created a human shield
A few hundred graduate students created a human shield around a nuclear site in Iran.
Through this gesture, they want to support their country’s nuclear program in the face of a possible Israeli assault.
The students began praying at noon in front of the site and then desired the death of the US and Israel.
A few hundred students from the universities of Isfahan created a human shield on Tuesday around the Isfahan Nuclear Technological Center where uranium is transformed.
Thus, they openly stated that they would defend their country's nuclear program at the risk of their own lives.
The International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) has found in its latest information that Iran has continued to strengthen its nuclear weapons.
There are reports in Israel of a possible attack on Iran's nuclear facilities.
The students began praying at noon in front of the site and then desired the death of the US and Israel.
In the case of an attack, whose objective would be to destroy Iran's nuclear program, the targets would not only be Isfahan, but also the Natanz site where uranium is enriched.
The feeding of an obese child: does not eat breakfast and takes cold cuts for dinner
More than a third of children aged 9 to 13 have overweight problems, 9% of schoolchildren will weigh above average and 5% are obese.
As current research shows, obese children come from families with an unhealthy lifestyle.
It shows once again the extent to which the environment in which the human being and the models around him is important.
On the tables of obese children there is, for example, cold cuts 50% more often than in families of children with normal weight.
19% of the obese had fries at dinner according to the survey carried out with an awareness action "Obesity is no coincidence"
In the families of the small large the sport is also not a habit, which is now the case of most of today's schoolchildren - only 15% responded that at least once a week parents found time for active movement.
Survey conducted on 900 children
The survey took place during the final school year and participated in 900 pupils from primary schools in the Czech Republic.
It was the second edition of "Obesity is not a coincidence", an action supported by General Health Insurance and Unilever.
Since the beginning it is more than 12000 students from sixth to third who have enrolled in this project.
One of the determinants that causes a dramatic increase in the number of overweight or even obese children is the absence of a proper diet and not enough physical exercise.
"Only half of the children questioned indicate for example eating 5 times a day breakfast-in case - lunch - snack - dinner, which is the basic principles of a good diet," says one of the results of the survey.
Without breakfast and charcutery at dinner
Specialists draw attention to the fact that in order to have a healthy development it takes a few basic details such as a family breakfast at the same time.
In the Czech Republic, only 23% of students’ families eat at the same time.
In the majority of families, everyone has breakfast alone.
And the worst that has been raised is that one-tenth of the population doesn't eat breakfast at all.
The breakfast is the basis of a good daily diet.
The questionnaire showed that in obese children’s families, unhealthy fries are consumed more often.
Almost every student – not to mention weight – drinks sugary drinks every day (70%).
More than 40% of the children questioned do sports regularly but for parents it is half, only 15%.
Preparing Your Food
Another part of the survey allowed selected children (204 boys and 172 girls from 13 schools) to prepare their own food from the possibilities offered according to their own taste and personal opinion.
"Preferences for Czech children between the ages of 12 and 15 are far from a healthy diet, from the ideal."
Among their favorite dishes there are a lot of cakes, meats and sweets.
"The most alarming is in particular a great preference for sweet lemonades," said in the results of the survey.
For lunch it was the pasta that took first place right in front of the white meat.
The children did not want starches at all and the preference for fish and vegetable meals was very low.
Focus on health
The survey also showed that children are willing to change their habits from the moment they receive ad hoc information.
"During a control of a group of survey participants who had completed the questionnaire after the "Obesity is not a coincidence" awareness session, a well-determined willingness to move towards a healthy diet," the results of the survey said.
For example, the most striking thing about sweet lemonads because children have begun to give preference to drinking water.
Childrens have most often ticked white meat and fish as the main course on the questionnaire and would reduce sweet and "knedliky" (Czech specialty of bread flour or potato dumplings).
The stylist must also be a good psychologist, the professionals say
In a presentation article about how to learn for stylists, I got a little bit angry about the fact that there were a lot from the beginning.
I wasn't thinking about what was going to happen afterwards.
The presentations of three professionals of the specialty, the clothing of the characters and a seminar on what is happening on site.
And that'll be worse.
The closer we get to the final exams, the more practical exercises and information await.
And even when there are classes on Saturdays and Sundays it's really "burned".
This time we have with Director Alenka (in the course there is no boy) dealing with how to dress the woman who does not have standard measurements.
Women of this type are the majority.
One has a small neck, the other a boy's body, without any particular curve, another of overweight.
The stylist must know how to optically ammenuize wide arms, prolong a neck or add necessary curves.
We have thus managed to emphasize beautifully the character and also not to dress in a too showy way types of women like Jennifer Lopez with a strong chest and pronounced hips and a thin waist.
For example, if there is a difference between the waist and the hips in such a way that skirts or trousers do not pass at all, it is worth being custom-made.
And you will not regret it because the clothing that falls impeccably is priceless.
In a tailor-made skirt you will feel much better than in the one that slides constantly, rolls up and does not fit the belt and so on.
For those who have a masculine appearance can afford a Tucker-style clothing, with pieces of sewn fabrics, or embroidery.
There are obviously many examples of various appearances and I am happy that I have all week to sort all the information received.
But I'm also afraid that given what I have to do at home there are too many.
Each intern received a celebrity to dress for the day and evening.
We have to take into consideration the current appearance, the type of personality mode as well as its appearance.
I'll have to "dress" Miranda Kerr, that maybe you know about the Victoria Secret campaign.
At the bottom of me, it pleases me, because it's better than to dress Britney Spears, Christina Aguilera who has gained almost a hundred pounds lately (don't take my statement, please, completely seriously) or the young Selena Gomez.
We have to cut and sew from the magazines or search on the internet, print and work the graphics.
Moodboard, as we say for the end result, expresses our personal style as well as our relationship with graphic design.
Also reflecting on the graphic part of styling is also important.
The stylist dresses not only the physicle but creates for example the productive pages in magazines (on products given the trends for handbags, coats, etc...).
Mario Kamenik, stylist and graphic designer, told us about all this.
But that... until Sunday
The stylist must have a general vision
Three guests of the specialty gave a diverse aspect to Saturday's session filled with information about the different types of characters.
Honza Pokorny, stylist, Jakub Polanka fashion graphic designer and Ben Renc, fashion photographer.
Jakub reminded us that fashion is an illusion and the stylist should know how to use it.
And a talented stylist knows how to work with a single clothing in a different way.
Variability is for this important example.
As for example this trench-coat which must be worn in a classic way with jeans and a t-shirt like a light coat but also it can also dress the bare body, with pumps and take it as a dress.
Or you just have to raise the sleeves or the collar and immediately have a new look.
“Play with that,” he said.
But I particularly appreciated the following advice: "For the job you need to know the rules perfectly".
"Then you can start contravening it," Jakub said.
Finally I understand why we try to learn these rules, what to do with, towards what, why, when in fashion magazines we sometimes see something else.
No statement on fashion shows.
I know again, thanks to fashion photographer Ben that the stylist must have many more clothing variants than those that are photographed.
That is to say that for fashion story which will have a dozen pages (so a dozen models) I must be ready to "retailing" at least fifteen.
And also, a garment and its combination with other elements appear completely differently than in reality.
We have to count with that in the course of creating a model.
The fact that the image and the style sometimes make half of the success was confirmed by Honza Pokorny.
Just look at Madonna who isn’t a great singer but her image and marketing have made her a global star.
In the Czech Republic, the approach to the use of the services of stylists remains cautious.
And known faces sometimes consider them useless (it’s enough for me to know something, but what I seem goes second).
And if someone gets styling on our part, then we have to rely on the fact that he dictates to us with great probability a completely different size (smaller) than the one he actually has.
We then have to browse Google and make sure if the boulevard news reports the celebrity in question, if it has lost weight or enlarged etc...
Honza and Mario asked us Sunday on the heart that it is not enough for the stylist to orient himself in fashion and know how to assemble models.
He must communicate with the people he dresses and it is thus important to be a good psychologist.
Knowing how to guess people, do not flatter, keep your opinion.
"When a manager asks you to sort her closet and fill it with new elements you can't throw everything away and tell her, God what a horror."
“You’ll find a few things you’ll find pretty and him you’ll recommend with what to wear them,” Mario says.
This one has shown us concretely what must contain everything called the "placovka" or bag of the stylist.
It’s the one you hang around the waist that you’re looking at yourself for everything you need.
In addition to things clearly defined as scissors, rollers for dispilation or nanny pins, there is also nylon thread (which the stylist uses to photograph products such as bags, or hats), special clips with which we close a garment in the back, if it is too large (the pin or other type of staple are not useable because they
So that we are not only people who listen but who have tried something in a practical way they have taught us how to properly reselect shoes.
And during the photo shoot in the workshop where the surface is equal, the sole could be damaged, especially outside.
And so we glued and glued.
We weren't allowed to touch the scissors so we wouldn't inadvertently injure.
So we really need skills.
Mario made me happy when he congratulated me for my creation.
The account I'm reporting isn't for my girlfriend.
This is only a small summary of what we have learned during the second weekend of classes
I’m starting to figure out more and more that making styling a profession isn’t a walk in a rose garden, that everyone says what they want.
The need for speed The Run argues throughout America.
Revision
Originally a trouble-free race is transformed because of a set of stupid mistakes of people who don't care in a routine morning trip to work.
It fulfills everyone's ambition to a certain extent, but it's useless if no one wants to do something more.
The new subtitled part The Run produced high expectations before its release.
He promised to take a new direction with the already-old Need for Speed racing series and release some kind of game from playable games that wouldn’t just count with points.
So we were curious how are going to be the added passages during which the main hero comes out of his car and does what he wants.
As is already done in the NFS series, the result is completely other than expected.
These are potentially arcade racing games, but the set pulls down because of some useless mistakes that have already existed for several years.
These aren't really mistakes but rather the expression of incomprehensible laziness on the part of developers.
The adventure begins very well.
You're caught up in the adventure whose main hero Jack has character issues and to solve them begins to participate in illegal races across America.
Sitting behind the wheel on the west coast in San Francisco and your mission is to arrive first in New York.
The idea has some interesting elements.
The route is divided into ten stages and then into more than 50 races.
As a result, each race takes place on another route and the planned stages in different environments that stand out quite well from each other and are interesting.
The player does not have the feeling for a moment that the game offers him something identical.
Some environments are also quite pretty even if the technical graphic level is of the same type as the previous series.
It's not the end of the world.
But driving through the desert, in autumn landscapes or in highly snow-capped mountains is very pleasing visually.
The tests are in addition from time to time embellished with an atypical element.
For example in the desert you find yourself in a sandstorm that significantly decreases your visibility.
Then in the mountains you have to be careful that an avalanche doesn't fall on you.
Besides this, the different races are well arranged one behind the others.
There are only a small number, but that's enough.
There are moments you strive to surpass the requested number of opponents (as in a classic race) then you run against the clock (classic duel with the stopwatch) and then still await you another duel with an opponent.
From time to time you also have the police who enter into the game and who are trying to make the situation tough.
The novelty is out-of-vehicle passages.
It’s more of an interactive animation when most of the time Jack runs away in front of someone and you have to help them by tapping on the right button at the right time.
There's nothing complicated.
What’s surprising is that there are less moments of this type than what you’re waiting for (to be concrete there are only three).
The result is like this because this element is not likely to hinder and is placed, in the context described above, in the elements that enhance the game.
The driving model is in the tradition of previous games.
Which means there's nothing extraordinary right now, but we can't say it's negative.
When it comes to realistic simulation you’ll need to go elsewhere.
But although we can find better in the competition the driving model goes very well with the type of design of the races.
So it's all okay.
Problems begin to appear after some time.
According to the driving model, that of collisions is not yet developed.
We don’t expect from this game complicated deformation and collisions, but when you don’t, in a collision with any object, the slightest idea of how your car behaves, so it’s not completely good.
During tight overflows you sometimes touch each other slightly but otherwise your car goes off in crazy aerobatics.
Or is in crumbs.
Thanks to the restarting system this is not really a problem but it really annoys you.
The restarting is done in such a way that when you broke your face or you have come out in the setting the game brings you back to the moment of the last point on the route.
However, you only have 5 restarts.
When you have used the 5 restarts you have to restart the game from the beginning.
So it's more of a tool, in case when something doesn't go the right, than something you can really rely on.
Sometimes the restarts do not help and we have to find the solution by remembering from memory the piece of route in question.
The great problem of this game is that the same actions are found in the same places.
For example, there are certain corners that you have to pass in a certain way otherwise it does not pass.
Otherwise you encounter on a given place "civil" vehicles always in the same configuration as you arrived first, fifth, 5 seconds in advance or one minute late.
What makes people angry are the situations when you easily see the opponent pass between two cars coming in the opposite direction and when you arrive, you, you either have to stand aside and conturnate them or brake.
It's equal if you go in front of him because it's "calculated" in such a way that for the given situation it always arrives very close to your nose.
Opponents still have other advantages.
Throughout the time of the game, you arrive in certain places, again without worrying about time, and you always have the same adversary that precedes you in the same place.
This pisses the most at the end of the game when you ride on a long deck in the opposite direction.
Adversary has to pass in front of you at all costs.
When it passes in front of you it hides the sight of the other vehicles in the opposite direction and you collide a good number of times.
It can be understood that the purpose of this game is to do something captivating and full of adredaline, but it is clear that you get bored quickly.
And it's a shame because through a simple driving model the game is interesting and the places with so much action that you don't have the time to follow everything that's going on.
And it's equal if it's because of the concept of 50 unique routes, that the order of races is such that there is no chance to get bored or something else.
The original idea is the change of car during the races.
You have to pay attention to gasoline pumps on routes because you can change cars there however most of the time the one you have is enough for you.
Cars are divided into three categories.
Sports cars are ideal for cities, large U.S. displacements for straight highways and super sports cars with exotic attire on very technical pipes for example on laced roads in the mountains.
And the mode of challenges, which are races in particular places that you know of the adventure, goes very well with the main diet of history.
You receive not only medals but also experience points that are added to your profile that is common to challenges and adventure.
When you have reached the highest level of driver, different objects begin to unlock:
It connects online with the Autolog feature which, among other things, compares your results obtained with those of other players and provides you with other functions in the community.
One of the most difficult blows to understand is the situation of the last adventure race.
You arrive with your car in the subway tunnel (it looks like) where you drive in the darkness on the lanes (it looks like).
Your speedometer shows you between 150 and 200 km/hour (a priori) and behind you arrives a subway train that sends you the car directly to scrap metal.
At the editorial office we had a discussion for a few days to know if someone has really thought about the creation of this game or if the authors really take us for idiots.
The technical part of the game is not extra, but the visual part is generally nice and in some cases really great.
What bothers is that in more extreme situations, imaging does not hold the level and in some cases in a tragic way.
This mainly concerns accidents with a large number of participants when fluid imaging is no longer useful.
The sound part is good and the track is of your choice.
In order to please the greatest number and especially the youngest audience a new sound track has been created in the style "I mix everything", but we can expect that no one will buy the game for music.
Need for Speed's overall impression: The Run is really confusing.
If the game didn't have these stupid mistakes we could say without fear that this is the best NFS production in recent years.
But this game gives the impression of not being finished.
The fun is really good but get ready for the faults to hit your eyes with the strength of an aerodrome reflector.
Velvet students in concert with Charles University choirs
The Festa Academica festival offers for the third time festivities that link the International Student Day with the anniversary of the Velvet Revolution with a musical part.
During the festival 20 choirs of graduate schools and secondary classes occur.
The highlight of the festival consists of two concerts held on 17 November.
"Charles University has an important part in this festival."
"Among the choirs there is the Choir of the Faculty of Pedagogy and Humanities, in the committee of the festival sits the rector Vaclav Hampl," says the head of the organizing team Jakub Calou.
The highlight of the festival is the concert of the choir of high schools and secondary classes which takes place with free entry on November 17 from 14 hours on the space located in front of the National Technical Library in Dejvice.
In the program there is the composition of the well-known Czech jazzman Karel Ruzicka, Celebration Jazz mass.
In the evening takes place the concert "Velvet students" in the premises of the National House in Vinohrady during which the choirs of the higher schools and that of Charles University perform.
Festa Academica aims not only to celebrate with dignity the International Day of Students and to recall the 22nd anniversary of the velvet revolution, but also to present to the public a choir music of the highest level and develop the creative cooperation of young people.
The main organizer is the Union of Chewers in cooperation with Jan Kepler High School.
All the action is under the aegis of Bohuslav Svoboda, Mayor of Prague and Vaclav Hampl, Rector of Charles University.
The festival takes place from 16 to 20 November in Prague and Pardubice.
The program offers high-level concerts, msical encounters, a student happening and other activities.
Interestees will find all the information on the festival's Internet pages www.festaacademica.cz.
Vicenova, Ambassador to the European Union:
The Czechs behave like negativists and Eurosceptics
"The Lisbon Treaty radically removed the balance between the institutions"
"I didn't expect such a hard war."
"It will last 5.6 years before the situation calms down and all the players become accustomed to their new role", this is how Miléna Vicenova began her presentation at the Faculty of Law the Czech ambassador near the European Union.
When she succeeded in describing the different bodies of the EU and their relations in such an understandable and visible way, to the point that a large number of lecturers from the Faculty of Law of Charles University could envy it, she showed how she takes her motto "comprehensible and openly about Europe" very seriously.
Mrs Vicenova paid tribute to the work of Herman Van Rompuye, the new Permanent President of the European Council.
"From the very beginning, critics resound that it is bland, that it is a leather round, that it cannot fill any mission and I have to say that it has taken the breath away from everyone because it holds its role to perfection."
"He is a man who knows how to listen to 27 member states, communicate well with them and has a clear vision of the management to take from Europe."
She explained the new post of the High Representative for Foreign Affairs and Defence Policy as part of an answer to the question: "Who is who in the European Union?" "To which telephone number should I call?", therefore as an important step towards uniqueness and a greater legibility of Union policy in relation to states, as is China or India.
Nobody wants to forbid us our syrecky (cooked cheese that smells very strong)
Mrs Vicenova has also mentioned the agenda that the European Council has lived, lives and will live in a similar time.
She described the Czech presidency two years ago as successful.
The Czechs have solved the rising financial crisis, the gas crisis or organized an Eastern Partnership Summit.
She described the fall of the government as very negative and damaged the image of the Czech Republic.
The Czech representation in the EU is currently very busy.
In the words of the Ambassador, "the activity has beaten its full place" not only for the Presidency but also for the financial crisis that continues to be resolved even now.
In addition, it is necessary to approve the Union's new septimal budget, which is becoming very complicated because of the current economic situation.
Since it would seem that the budget will be slim and with a view to economies, which branch will have the priority, which countries will be helped the most, the least, everything needs to be solved in the context of future negotiations.
The Ambassador recalled her slogans with which she arrived in Brussels "For an understandable Europe".
“I really don’t like abbreviations, foreign words, jargons that nobody understands.
As the citizen must understand that it is true that in Brussels no one makes round or twisted pickles, bananas differently large or that no one has forbidden us to make syrecky."
It wants to make better use of the EU's environment and see more Czechs in the European institutions.
A multi-speed Europe awaits us
According to the Ambassador the Czechs have the reputation of being Eurosceptics and people who only see things in their negative aspect more than positively.
In addition she is sorry to see such a small Czech representation in the European institutions.
According to her, the fault stems from several factors, such as the timidity of our candidates, their inability to write a cover letter and weak support from the Czech side.
In addition to a successful Czech Presidency, it then underlined the strength and cooperation of the Visegrad Group.
"Believe me, when come to me the Pole, the Magyar, the Slovak, this Frenchman says to me: 'Hey, what are you doing there, what does this Visegrad group still do?' and he's not at all happy.'"
According to Mrs Vicenova, in the near future there are new tough rules on fiscal policy awaiting member countries.
It is the concept of a two-speed Europe, if not at multiple speeds, which prevails rather than a "new European Federation".
"We have countries in the eurozone and others outside the zone."
"We have the Schengen area, we also have the Institute for Enhanced Cooperation."
In the first place it was said that the countries that want them and those who don’t want to cooperate among themselves remain in their corners.”
"There will be a lot of institutes of this type and there will be a truly two-speed Europe," Vicenova said.
From this point of view it also appreciated the mission of the Czech Republic and Herman Van Rompuye to determine the basis that all issues having an impact on the EU should be debated among all members of the EU and not only the members of the eurozone.
History of a Brand:
Innovator IBM begins the second century of its existence
If someone had to look for the word that expresses the IBM strategy as closely as possible, the closest one would be "the long term".
For a large audience IBM is the symbol of the technological revolution, is a firm felt as very current and yet since its creation it has passed a hundred years.
The basis of this long-term strategy has been thrown away by the firm’s first leader, visionary Thomas J. Watson Sr.
He lefted this slogan that a large number of global problems can be resolved if people are eager to think.
Its slogan "PENSE'!" has become the imprint around which the life of a future giant will develop (and also the title of the internal magazine that IBM began editing in 1935).
This was the basis of the company's culture of caring developed by Watson.
For us IBM means a long-term thought of continuous movements directed towards the future.
IBM survived a hundred years thanks to the fact that it always remained true to its core values and yet was not afraid to change everyone else around it.
This allowed us in our first century to transform technology, business and society.
We hope that in the second century we will reach even more," said the current director of Samuel J. Palmisano for the anniversary.
A well-prepared system
Watson, in the 1930s, began caring for his employees like Bata in the Czech Republic - the people of IBM were the only ones among the first U.S. employees to have paid vacations, employer-paid insurance plus an elegant employee uniform and a well-crafted system of rewards for inventors and salespeople.
In the same way, IBM has a well-crafted system of customer relationships.
At the beginning, the company was brilliant in the discovery of talents – as one of the first firms to have abolished any form of discrimination and thus could have the choice.
The current plan is completely in the spirit of anti-discriminatory strategy since it will be a woman - Virginia Rometty - who should replace Palmisano at the head of IBM.
She has worked at IBM for thirty years and is currently Head of Sales, Marketing and Strategy.
IBM in recent years has done so-called jamy, online brain-storming from which a lot of future strategies and innovations come from.
It’s no wonder he has a lot of ideas – in the firm there are nearly 500,0000 people working.
An institution with a good name
It is the internal and external image of the company that ensures it a safe position in the business field.
“Since the beginning IBM had a concept of an institution rather than a technology firm,” said Rosabeth Moss Kanter, professor of economics at the Harvard School of Economics and author of the book on IBM.
"IBM is not a technological firm but a firm that helps solve problems in the business world using its technology," added Geogre Colony of the consulting firm Forrester Research.
As the firm itself says there is a difference between entering the market and creating this market.
IBM - or the "Big Blue", as it is colloquially called in the United States with regard to its slogan - in a hundred years it has grown to become one of the world's largest firms.
It is obviously the most versatile technological firm - it develops software, hardware, infrastructure, hosting, consulting services at the level of products from the server to nanotechnology.
She holds numerous patents from all U.S. tech firms and five of her employees have received a Nobel Prize.
Among his discoveries is for example the ATM, the payment card, the financial swap, the bar code or the diskette.
IBM ended up this year with US$220 billion the second largest technology firm according to the capitalization of the market (the first is Apple), when for the first time it surpassed Microsoft in 1996.
Preview in advance
These are not all innovations and fabrications that had the preference of the customer and of the time - IBM for example did not pass the bet on an operating system own OS/2, the Prodige online service or the IBM PCjr computer:
"From the moment your business is built on the movement in advance you can't emotionally stand on the past," remarks Samuel J. Palmisano.
For this IBM has no problem building its foundations on a lot of platforms and when they don't work it leaves.
Unlike, for example, the Microsoft competitor, which at the base stands and remains under the Windows operating system.
A technology perspective
In IBM revenues, services, which are trained for one-fifth by software and hardware, have a prominent place.
However, still in 1990 it was with more of the motto of participation the strongest representative of hardware.
From the year 2000 IBM sold low-yield assets for US$15 billion, during that period it invested US$58 billion in the purchase of outlook technologies.
It continues in investment and even from 2008, when for the first time it surpassed the new financial crisis.
IBM is negotiating according to the precepts of its first leader Thomas J. Watson, who during the great economic crisis has also increased its investment volume.
It now appears that IBM is going through the current crisis without being worried?
The price of the IMB share has grown from 2008 in rocket by 120 percent, the firm's net profit continues to grow.
The logo of IMB is to change everything but not its values.
We can expect that this flexible giant will control other crises.
History of IMB: From the slices of cheeses to flights in the cosmos.
IBM (International Business Machines) was born in New York a hundred years ago; it originally had the complicated name Computing Tabulating Recording Corporation.
It took the name IBM in 1924 - initially it was a brand used by a branch of a firm in Canada and South America.
The basis of the future IBM was the merger of four firms whose history is linked to the 80's of the ninteenth century.
They possessed technologies such as for example the former "pointers", the clocks that recorded the arrival and departure of employees.
The architect of the new company was Charles Ranlett Flint who until 1930 presided over the Supervisory Board of the company.
Flint hired the head of a competing firm Thomas J. Watson to help him run the company.
The leader then overshadowed the firm’s founder—it is upon Watson’s ideas that society’s identity and culture have been based until now.
Watson ran the firm until 1952.
IBM, as its name says, began with the production of all possible machinery for business and trade - from cheese and meat slicers to the cash register.
In the first four years when Watson led, revenue multiplied up to US$9 million and began the firm’s expansion in all parts of the world.
Watson was so irreplaced for the firm that after 40 years of management it was his son who occupied the chair of director, Thomas Watson Junior.
Under his direction IBM began the development of artificial intelligence and developed the first programming language.
In the 60's IBM people and computers helped NASA guide flights in the cosmos - on Mercury, Saturn, and in 1969 flight to the Moon.
Meanwhile in 1964, IBM developed the first family of computers - the IBM System/360.
The classic PC that determined the computer standard of the time with the name IBM 5150 came to market in 1981.
Twenty years later IBM sold its computer factory to the Chinese company Lenovo, but bought the consulting company Pricewaterhouse Coopers and began to take care of consulting and services with high added value.
IBM’s strategy over the past three years – is the Smarter Planet concept “a smarter planet.”
Its objective is the intelligent use of technology in areas not yet exploited such as the transport and management of cities.
In terms of the field of IMB commerce, an "Smarter Commerce" platform recently developed which helps salespeople to manage the entire trading cycle.
IBM also has a strong history in our territory.
It established its branch in Czechoslovakia in 1932 at the first country in Central and Eastern Europe.
Today, in addition to IBM RT, there is also Brno’s strategic outsourcing hub.
The Central for Central and Eastern Europe is headquartered in Prague and there is also the research and development team at the global level that deals with the recognition of speech.
Rychtarova about her unfaithful husband:
Ivette you can keep this donkey, I don't want it anymore!
Darina Rychtarova (53) said, it's over!
After her husband Joseph Rychtar (53) became a bodyguard and lover of Iveta Bartosova (45), Darina still hoped that Joseph would wake up from his pink dream and return home.
Only she couldn't wait and established clear rules for future life.
"Pepa can come back home, but not like my partner," Rychtarova explained.
When Darina Rychtarova gave Bartosova asylum in the summer in her house, she had no idea that her couple would not hold.
When Iveta after 30 days insisted on relocating from Ricany, Pepa didn't push the singer back.
He confessed in public that he loved him.
With time Darina resigned herself, accepted her husband's affair and ended up saying goodbye forever.
Rychtirova is not interested to know who her husband sleeps with.
If Rychtar and Bartosova separate there will be no wife to welcome him on the doorstep of the house.
"He's the biological father of my sons and if he wants to end his life in our common house, no one will kick him out."
“He won’t be my old donkey loved and lost anymore, but a man with whom I have a special relationship,” Rychtarova filtered, pointing out that she detached herself from her husband but that they only remain in a decent relationship.
The fact that Darina closed the door to him is not a problem for Joseph.
“I respect my wife’s decision.”
"I'll stay with Iveta and won't change."
"My wife set up a wedding on paper and I respect it."
"The company continues, I take care of the repairs, the garden, the real estate, I buy."
"With Darina we discuss in a completely normal way but we don't sleep together," Rychtar told Blesk.
If Rychtarova finds a new love he won't stop it.
"We don't sleep together and I don't want to know where she's going, with whom and if she's having an affair.
I know it's my fault, I fell in love with "Iveta and I'm taking all the responsibility on me", concluded Joseph.
The Worst Vices of Women: Does that affect you too?
If you ask men to determine typical vices of women, all of them like any other, are able to get them out of their sleeves.
My dear ladies, you are going to know in the following lines of the female vices that manage to pump the blood from the veins of men.
Purchasing
Your other half gives you remarks that you are dependent on purchases?
Do you need to buy at least one garment a week?
Are you happy to buy and in packets at the time of sales?
In your case we can talk about purchases as a defect.
Some women think they should restrict their passion for shopping.
But you will say, which one would resist the shobby-logging of clothing stores, to look for for yourself nice clothes and then try them all in the cabin (the ideal of different colors)?
And although for most women buying is a hobby, it can become for the man a real hell.
Just remember how many times did you tell your spouse that they're waiting at the entrance...
Constuent dissatisfaction
"I'm not too big"?
"I'd need to lose weight at least 5 pounds - I should start exercising?"
"Do you like it?"
Don't these sentences remind you of something?
Yes? Yeah.
So you're one of those women who's obsessed with their appearance.
That’s not the question that you should stop taking care of yourself, but a large number of men are allergic to the fact that their partner is always complaining about his appearance.
Strong sex doesn’t hesitate to say that the higher the frequency of these complaints increases, the more poisonous women become.
Odre and cleanliness in first place
It's like an infinite carousel.
Wash the windows, vacuum, clean the floors, make the dust, strip the bathroom - and this twice a week.
You make remarks to your partner that he walks with dirty feet on the clean floor, to the children that they have soiled the sink, clogged the window of the living room, and it gives you a lot of work?
In case you suffer precisely from this obsession, try to keep in mind that we should not exaggerate anything and that order and cleanliness should not be in the first place in the family.
However, this harmless desire for cleanliness can ruin your relationships and even family peace.
The work of undermining
"Put this worn-out tracksuit in the trash."
"Are you going to wear these old socks again tomorrow?"
"A wet towel has nothing to do on the floor."
If you do on your partner this job this way several times a day, you’re really going to decompose it.
It is obvious that you do not think badly you want everything to be impeccable.
Maybe if men knew it, women wouldn't have to do so much understock...
Defamation, persiflage
Defamation, persiflage but also insults against someone are also the own of some women.
Women are driven especially to relationships and so are happy to deal with topics like who, where, with whom, how and why.
Maybe each of us leaves a small harmless persifling here and there.
The hand on the heart is a peculiarity of women.
But the worst are those who advise, persiflate, even despise others and are for their entourage - especially at work in a collective of women - particularly dangerous.
